From 1111111111111111111111111111111111111111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Tia <anthropic@jetm.me>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] rzv2h-dev: boot Avocado extlinux from SD, not vendor
 ext4/booti

The Avocado image (stone) provisions a FAT boot partition carrying
extlinux.conf, the kernel Image and the RDK dtb, plus an erofs rootfs
addressed by PARTUUID. The vendor CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND instead runs
`ext4load mmc 0:2 boot/Image` + booti against a single ext4 rootfs with a
fixed EVK dtb name, so it cannot boot the Avocado layout at all.

Point CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND at sysboot (CONFIG_CMD_SYSBOOT, already enabled)
to parse extlinux.conf on the FAT boot partition (partition 1), trying
mmc 1 then mmc 0 so it does not depend on which controller the microSD
enumerates on.

The load addresses partition the 0x48000000-0x58000000 bootm window so
that pxe_utils' three loads cannot overlap. label_boot() loads kernel,
then initrd, then fdt at these addresses and checks none of them against
each other, so every window has to be wide enough on its own:

  fdt_addr_r     0x48000000 -> 0x48080000    512 KiB
  kernel_addr_r  0x48080000 -> 0x4c000000    63.5 MiB
  ramdisk_addr_r 0x4c000000 -> 0x57000000    176 MiB
  scriptaddr     0x57000000 -> 0x58000000    16 MiB

kernel_addr_r and fdt_addr_r keep the vendor booti values. The initrd
window is what the vendor flow never exercised: ext4load + booti loaded
no ramdisk, so the vendor's spacing says nothing about a layout that
always has one. An arm64 Image from a cip vendor config runs 30-40 MiB,
which does not fit under the 0x4a000000 this patch first used.

Build-verified only: the sysboot path/prefix, mmc index and load
addresses are board-specific and must be confirmed at the u-boot prompt
on real hardware.

Slot A only. sysboot is pinned at partition 1, which is boot-a, so the
gpt-ab strategy the stone manifest declares cannot yet boot or roll back
into boot-b. Reaching both slots means letting the shared Renesas
CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND fragment's distro_bootcmd scan the EF00 partitions
instead of hardcoding a second command here, which is a separate change:
it needs the vendor #define removed rather than replaced, and it needs
the fastboot fallback token in that fragment scoped off this machine
first, since fastboot no longer builds here.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Avocado board integration]
Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <anthropic@jetm.me>
---
 include/configs/rzv2h-dev.h | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/configs/rzv2h-dev.h b/include/configs/rzv2h-dev.h
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/include/configs/rzv2h-dev.h
+++ b/include/configs/rzv2h-dev.h
@@ -80,7 +80,11 @@
 	"bootcmd_check=if mmc dev 1; then run sd1load; else run sd0load; fi \0"
 #endif
 
-#define CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND	"env default -a;run bootcmd_check;run bootimage"
+#define CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND \
+	"setenv scriptaddr 0x57000000; setenv kernel_addr_r 0x48080000; " \
+	"setenv fdt_addr_r 0x48000000; setenv ramdisk_addr_r 0x4c000000; " \
+	"sysboot mmc 1:1 any ${scriptaddr} /extlinux/extlinux.conf; " \
+	"sysboot mmc 0:1 any ${scriptaddr} /extlinux/extlinux.conf"
 
 /* For board */
 /* Ethernet RAVB */
